<spell-page "dimension usage" notebook>
	<header level="1">
		Dimension
		<header>A dimension shows one measure in the reader's own units:  5 ft 8 in in the US, 172 cm elsewhere.</>
	</>
	<section>
		<toolbar class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#overview">Overview</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Overview">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-dimension>` shows one measure in the reader's own units.

			- `value` is its number, in `unit`:  `cm`, `kg`, `°F`, by any of the unit's names.
			- `dimension` says what it measures:  `length`, `weight`, `temperature`, `volume`, `speed` or `proportion`.
			- A proportion is a percent:  kept as its fraction, `0.18`, and shown with its % sign the reader's way, `18%`.
			- A US reader sees feet and inches, pounds, °F and cups;  everyone else the metric unit nearest in size.
			- `in` asks for units of its own, largest first:  `in="feet and inches"`.
			- In Spell, `<ui-dimension value={its height}>` is told what its value measures:  its property says.
		</>
	</>
</spell-page>
